  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "The top-4 results (config_042, 013, 049, 002) all use scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer, with the best being 0.7250 (vit_l, weighted). The consistent pattern shows scvi_n200 >> scgpt, transformer >> avgpool, and weighted ≥ concat. However, no experiment has tested whether the multiprofile + transformer aggregation pipeline is actually adding value over a simpler singleprofile architecture. Config_006 pairs the best-known RNA encoder (scvi_n200), best image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and best fusion (weighted) with singleprofile (no aggregation step). This directly tests whether the added complexity of transformer-based multiprofile aggregation is contributing to the 0.7250 performance or whether a cleaner single-profile pathway could match or exceed it. With only 2 experiments remaining after this one, this is the highest-value exploration: it uses all the best-confirmed components while resolving a key architectural uncertainty, and a positive result would open a new direction to exploit in the final experiment."
}

